In article <1991Feb19.205631.15341@chinet.chi.il.us> prb@chinet.chi.il.us (Paul Botts) writes:
>3) Is there a reason for the right hand/left hand question when putting
>on a ring? If not, it ought to be removed. All unnecessary prompts and
>"-more-" lines should be removed.
I agree with this one. I don't think there is a difference between right-
or left ring finger, so there is no real point in asking. Maybe another
NETHACKOPTION should be defined to select the preferred first ring-finger.

>4) Is there a reason for having two different commands for donning armor
>and rings/amulets? If not, combine them into a single "wear" command.
Again I agree, just a Wear and Take off will do for armor/rings/amulets and
blindfolds.

>5) There should be a way to get an inventory list of all the items in a
>pile you`re standing on.
I assume you mean a list like you get when you type 'I'nventory ? With this
I agree. Also this should be working for sacks/bags & chests.

>6) When you try to wield, wear, put on, take off, remove, eat, apply,
>read, quaff, zap, Zap, throw something, the list of the appropriate
>items in your pack should be automatically displayed (like if you done
>I-whatever). This could be an option which could be turned off by people
>annoyed by it, but the default should be ON.
Hmm, this is only useful when playing on a system with enough performance.
If you play via a modem or slow system, this will be annoying, especially
when throwing a series of darts or arrows. I think the default should be OFF.

>7) The / command, to look at something, should be cleaned up. It has too
>many keystrokes involved in it currently (too many -more- things).
Agreed. One improvement would be to implement also the 'HJKLUYNB', another
would be to let the cursor jump to the next creature on the level by a single
keystroke. Maybe there should be an easy way to get a list of all visible
creatures on the current level
